yout 100 G (200 − 100 deductible, no special clause)\");\n\n  // === Claim: Dragon material ===\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G — payout 700 G (800 − 100 deductible)\");\n\n  // === Claim: High enchantment threshold >= 8 ===\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse steel sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 G at 50% — payout 400 G (500 − 100 deductible)\");\n\n  // === Claim: Dragon material AND high enchantment (both clauses, 50% wins) ===\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse steel sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 G — payout 400 G (500 − 100 deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse dragon-material sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 G — 50% applies (500), then deductible (400)\");\n\n  // === Claim: Dragon + high enchantment exactly at threshold ===\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse dragon-material sword enchantment exactly 8 damage 1000 G — 500 G (50%) − 100 = 400 G payout\");\n\n  // === Claim: Deductible per damage event ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply deductible per damaged item — dragon attack on sword (500) and amulet (300): payout 600 G (400 + 200)\");\n\n  // === Claim: Cap ===\n  it.todo(\"should compute cap for sword-only policy — insurance sum 1000 G, cap 2000 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should compute cap based on insurance sum (not premium) — cursed sword (insurance value 1000 G), cap 2000 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should compute insurance sum for sword + amulet: 1600 G, cap 3200 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should exhaust cap over two successive claims — first claim 1500 G -> payout 1400 G, remaining 600 G; second claim 1500 G -> payout 600 G, remaining 0 G\");\n\n  // === Claim: Multiple items of same type ===\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim when damages has more entries of a type than policy covers\");\n\n  // === Claim: Error cases ===\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim referencing unknown item type\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim with negative amount\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim for item not in policy\");\n\n  // === Multi-step scenario ===\n  it.todo(\"should handle multi-step scenario — quote then claim\");\n\n  // === CLI ===\n  it.todo(\"should produce correct JSON from stdin for schema example\");\n});"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":565,"output":2174,"cacheRead":12032,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14771,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950145561,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-27ff1d8f-9b95-4c54-84d1-239b9813c202","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ba4149fcd5fb4107995be959","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 6444 bytes to /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-28-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950154373},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Test List Created:\n**Feature**: MHPCO Claim Office — quote and claim operations\n**Test File**: `src/claim-office.spec.ts`\n**Tests**: 39\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple -> complex):\n1. Base premium for single sword — 105 G\n2. Base premium for single amulet — 65 G\n3. Base premium for single staff — 85 G\n4. Base premium for single potion — 45 G\n5. Single rune — 30 G\n6. Single moonstone — 30 G\n7. 2 runes (no block) — 55 G\n8. 3 runes (block) — 65 G\n9. 4 runes (no block) — 105 G\n10. 7 runes — 180 G\n11. 2 runes + 1 moonstone (different types, no block) — 80 G\n12. 3 runes + 3 moonstones (two blocks) — 125 G\n13. Cursed surcharge on single item — 155 G\n14. Cursed surcharge item-specific on multi-item policy — 215 G\n15. High enchantment (≥5) surcharge — 135 G\n16. No high enchantment below threshold — 105 G\n17. Both cursed and high enchantment — 185 G\n18. Loyalty discount at exactly 2 years — 85 G\n19. Loyalty discount at 3 years — 85 G\n20. No loyalty at 1 year — 105 G\n21. First