ver two successive claims — first claim 1500 G -> payout 1400 G, remaining 600 G; second claim 1500 G -> payout 600 G, remaining 0 G\");\n\n  // === Claim: Multiple items of same type ===\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim when damages has more entries of a type than policy covers\");\n\n  // === Claim: Error cases ===\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim referencing unknown item type\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim with negative amount\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim for item not in policy\");\n\n  // === Multi-step scenario ===\n  it.todo(\"should handle multi-step scenario — quote then claim\");\n\n  // === CLI ===\n  it.todo(\"should produce correct JSON from stdin for schema example\");\n});"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950197035},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me understand the current state. There's only 1 passing test, and the implementation is a hardcoded return. Let me run the tests to confirm they're all green:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0f05160c59d14b9986d44405","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-28-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro && pnpm test 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":2309,"output":153,"cacheRead":6144,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":8606,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950197036,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-92b20882-a686-4c1d-b9db-cda078bd9d43","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0f05160c59d14b9986d44405","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-28-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-2