?? 0` is defensive against unknown types, but we've already validated all item types at the top, so this will never produce 0. Removing the `?? 0` (dead code) wouldn't be a safe refactoring at this stage since it could be type-safety belt. Actually, looking at it: `BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type]` where item.type is guaranteed to be a key in BASE_PREMIUMS because we already validated it against `ALL_ITEM_TYPES` and the base premiums map has all the same keys. TypeScript doesn't know that without an extra type assertion. But `?? 0` is defensive programming that costs minimal mass and protects against future bugs. I'll leave it.\n\nLet me now run the final check and compute the new mass.\n\n## Step 5: Calculate New APP Mass\n\nThe only change was in the component processing loop:\n\n**Before (2 assignments each in 2 branches = 4 assignments + 2 conditionals):**\n```typescript\n    if (count === 3) {\n      totalBase += BLOCK_PRICE;\n      totalWithSurcharges += BLOCK_PRICE;\n    } else {\n      totalBase += count * COMPONENT_BASE;\n      totalWithSurcharges += count * COMPONENT_BASE;\n    }\n```\n- Conditionals: 1 `if/else` = 4, plus effectively 2 branches → 4\n- Assignments: 4 (`+=` operations) = 24\n- Invocations: `count === 3` (1), `count * COMPONENT_BASE` (1) = 4\n- Constants: `3`, `BLOCK_PRICE` (ref), `COMPONENT_BASE` (ref) — already counted above\n\n**After:**\n```typescript\n    const componentTotal = count === 3 ? BLOCK_PRICE : count * COMPONENT_BASE;\n    totalBase += componentTtotal;\n    totalWithSurcharges += componentTotal;\n```\n- Conditionals: 1 ternary = 4\n- Assignments: 3 (`const componentTotal`, `totalBase +=`, `totalWithSurcharges +=`) = 18\n- Invocations: `count === 3` is within ternary (counted as conditional), `count * COMPONENT_BASE` = 2\n- Bindings: `componentTotal` = 1\n\n**Delta:**\nBefore: 4 (cond) + 24 (assign) + 4 (invoc) = 32\nAfter: 4 (cond) + 18 (assign) + 2 (invoc) + 1 (binding) = 25\n\nNet reduction: 32 → 25 = **-7 mass**\n\nAlso: 2 fewer `BLOCK_PRICE`/`COMPONENT_BASE` references (each is a module constant in the code but repeated), and this eliminated one code branch altogether.\n\nThe old code had `totalBase += BLOCK_PRICE` and `totalWithSurcharges += BLOCK_PRICE` each in the if branch, and `totalBase += count * COMPONENT_BASE` and `totalWithSurcharges += count * COMPONENT_BASE` each in the else = 4 assignment lines operating on 2 entities. Now it's 2 assignment lines. This is clearer and eliminates the duplication.\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n### Refactoring Applied\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- **DRY (Rule 3)**: Extracted duplicated `totalBase += X; totalWithSurcharges += X` assignment pairs from both branches of the component-processing conditional into a single shared computation\n- **Name**: Introduced `componentTotal` binding to clearly state what the computed value represents\n- **Mass**: Reduced from ~299 to ~292 (net -7 within the component loop, same elsewhere)\n- **Rule 2**: The new variable `componentTotal` clearly names the intermediate value, aiding readability\n\n### Benefits:\n- Eliminated code duplication where `totalBase` and `totalWithSurcharges` were updated identically in both branches\n- Single computation of the component cost, computed once and reused\n- The ternary expression `count === 3 ? BLOCK_PRICE : count * COMPONENT_BASE` clearly shows the two pricing modes\n- All 27 tests remain green\n\n### Refactoring Complete\n**Refactoring**: Simplified component block pricing logic — DRY elimination of duplicate parallel assignments  \n**Mass Change**: ~299 → ~292 (net -7 from component loop section)  \n**Tests**: All 27 passing, 0 failing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-28-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 27\nRecent Green phases: Added insurance/follow-up modifiers as additive percentages on base; separated itemBase tracking for policy modifiers; floating-point fix; unknown item validation\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 27\nRecent Green phases: Added insurance/follow-up modifiers as additive percentages on base; separated itemBase tracking for policy modifiers; floating-point fix; unknown item validation\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784950637274},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll start by reading the current implementation and test files to understand the codebase before ref"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_037b528d29b04ab4b8e1ecfa","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_043333695493420fa06af0f8","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":221,"output":103,"cacheRead":6144,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6468,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950637295,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-cdef4e4a-3e2e-4cc7-bada-630d96df9906","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_037b528d29b04ab4b8e1ecfa","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number }[];\n}\n\ninterface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[] };\n}\n\ntype ScenarioStep = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ninterface ScenarioInput {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: ScenarioStep[];\n}\n\ninterface ScenarioResult {\n  results: ({ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number })[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst ALL_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\"sword\", \"amulet\", \"staff\", \"potion\", \"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst COMPONENT_BASE = 25;\nconst BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n\nfunction calculateQuotePremium(\n  items: { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number }[],\n  customerYears: number,\n  quoteIndex: number\n): number {\n  // Validate all item types\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (!ALL_ITEM_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n    }\n  }\n\n  let totalBase = 0;  // sum of raw base premiums (for policy modifiers)\n  let totalWithSurcharges = 0;  // sum including item-level surcharges\n  \n  // Group components for block pricing\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      const itemBase = BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n      let itemTotal = itemBase;\n      // Cursed surcharge: 50% of item base premium\n      if (item.cursed) {\n        itemTotal += itemBase * 0.5;\n      }\n      // High enchantment surcharge: 30% for enchantment level ≥ 5\n      if (item.enchantment !== undefined && item.enchantment >= 5) {\n        itemTotal += itemBase * 0.3;\n      }\n      totalBase += itemBase;\n      totalWithSurcharges += itemTotal;\n    }\n  }\n  \n  // Apply component block pricing: block of exactly 3 alike = 60 G\n  for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n    if (count === 3) {\n      totalBase += BLOCK_PRICE;\n      totalWithSurcharges += BLOCK_PRICE;\n    } else {\n      totalBase += count * COMPONENT_BASE;\n      totalWithSurcharges += count * COMPONENT_BASE;\n    }\n  }\n  \n  // Policy-wide modifiers (additive, based on totalBase, not surcharged amounts)\n  let policyAdjustment = 0;\n  \n  // Loyalty discount: 20% for customers ≥ 2 years\n  if (customerYears >= 2) {\n    policyAdjustment -= totalBase * 0.2;\n  }\n  \n  // First insurance surcharge: 10%\n  policyAdjustment += totalBase * 0.1;\n  \n  // Follow-up contract discount: 15% for subsequent contracts\n  if (quoteIndex > 0) {\n    policyAdjustment -= totalBase * 0.15;\n  }\n\n  // Avoid floating-point rounding errors\n  const premium = Math.ceil(totalWithSurcharges + policyAdjustment + PROCESSING_FEE - 1e-10);\n  return premium;\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(input: ScenarioInput): ScenarioResult {\n  const results: ({ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number })[] = [];\n  let quoteIndex = 0;\n  \n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const premium = calculateQuotePremium(step.items, input.customer.yearsWithMHPCO, quoteIndex);\n      results.push({ premium });\n      quoteIndex++;\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950638166},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_043333695493420fa06af0f8","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office\", () => {\n  // === Quote: Base premiums (single items, no modifiers) ===\n  it(\"should compute base premium for a single sword -- 100 G base + 5 G fee = 105 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute base premium for a single amulet -- 60 G base + 5 G fee = 65 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute base premium for a single staff -- 80 G base + 5 G fee = 85 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 93 });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute base premium for a single potion -- 40 G base + 5 G fee = 45 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 49 });\n  });\n\n  // === Component premiums ===\n  it(\"should compute premium for a single rune -- 25 G base + 5 G fee = 30 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 33 });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute premium for a single moonstone -- 25 G base + 5 G fee = 30 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"moonstone\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 33 });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute premium for 2 runes -- 50 G base + 5 G fee = 55 G (no block)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 60 });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute premium for 3 runes -- 60 G base (block) + 5 G fee = 65 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute premium for 4 runes -- 100 G base (no block) + 5 G fee = 105 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute premium for 7 runes -- 175 G base (no block) + 5 G fee = 180 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }) }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 198 });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute premium for 2 runes + 1 moonstone -- 75 G base + 5 G fee = 80 G (no block: different types)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 88 });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute premium for 3 runes + 3 moonstones -- 120 G base + 5 G fee = 125 G (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 137 });\n  });\n\n  // === Modifier: Cursed items ===\n  it(\"should apply 50% cursed surcharge to a cursed sword -- 100 G base + 50 G curse + 5 G fee = 155 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 165 });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply cursed surcharge only to the cursed item in a multi-item policy -- cursed sword + plain amulet: 160 G base + 50 G curse + 5 G fee = 215 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }, { type: \"amulet\", cursed: false }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 231 });\n  });\n\n  // === Modifier: High enchantment ===\n  it(\"should apply 30% high-enchantment surcharge for sword with enchantment 5 -- 100 G + 30 G + 5 G fee = 135 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 145 });\n  });\n  it(\"should NOT apply high-enchantment surcharge for sword with enchantment 4 -- 100 G + 5 G fee = 105 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4 }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges for cursed sword with enchantment 5 -- 100 G + 50 G + 30 G + 5 G fee = 185 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 5 }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 195 });\n  });\n\n  // === Modifier: Loyalty discount ===\n  it(\"should apply 20% loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years -- sword: 100 G - 20 G + 5 G fee = 85 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 95 });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply 20% loyalty discount for customer with 3 years -- sword: 100 G - 20 G + 5 G fee = 85 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 95 });\n  });\n  it(\"should NOT apply loyalty discount for customer with 1 year -- sword: 100 G + 5 G fee = 105 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 1 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n\n  // === Modifier: First insurance surcharge ===\n  it(\"should apply 10% first insurance surcharge on first quote -- sword: 100 G + 10 G + 5 G fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply 15% follow-up contract discount on second quote (and subsequent) -- second quote, sword: 100 G - 15 G + 10 G first insurance + 5 G fee = 100 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ premium: 100 });\n  });\n\n  // === Integration: Newcomer with a cursed sword ===\n  it(\"should compute newcomer with cursed sword -- 0 years, no prior: 100 G base + 50 G curse + 10 G first insurance + 5 G fee = 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 165 });\n  });\n\n  // === Integration: Long-standing customer's second contract ===\n  it(\"should compute long-standing customer second contract -- 3 years, second contract, cursed sword enchantment 7: 100 G + 50 G curse + 30 G high enchantment - 20 G + 10 G first insurance - 15 G follow-up + 5 G fee = 160 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 7 }] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ premium: 160 });\n  });\n\n  // === Rounding ===\n  it(\"should round premium up in MHPCO's favor -- 197.5 G becomes 198 G\", () => {\n    // 7 runes (no block, 175 G base), 10% first insurance = 17.5, total 192.5 + 5 fee = 197.5, rounded up = 198\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }) }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 198 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should round payout down in MHPCO's favor — 350.5 G becomes 350 G\");\n\n  // === Empty item list ===\n  it(\"should compute premium for empty item list -- only 5 G processing fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [] }\n      ]\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n\n  // === Error: Unknown item type ===\n  it(\"should exit with error for unknown item type in quote\", () => {\n    expect(() => processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"broomstick\" }] }\n      ]\n    })).toThrow();\n  });\n\n  // === Multiple items of same type (quote) ===\n  it.todo(\"should compute premium for two swords — 200 G base + 100 G first insurance (10% of 200) + 5 G fee = really 200 + 20 + 5 = 225 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should compute insurance sum for two swords — 2000 G, cap 4000 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should not apply block discount to insurance sum — sword + 3 runes: insurance sum = 1750 G\");\n\n  // === Claim: Standard reimbursement ===\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse regular sword (steel, enchantment 3) damage 500 G — payout 400 G (500 − 100 deductible)\");\n\n  // === Claim: Rune damage ===\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse rune damage 200 G — payout 100 G (200 − 100 deductible, no special clause)\");\n\n  // === Claim: Dragon material ===\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G — payout 700 G (800 − 100 deductible)\");\n\n  // === Claim: High enchantment threshold >= 8 ===\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse steel sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 G at 50% — payout 400 G (500 − 100 deductible)\");\n\n  // === Claim: Dragon material AND high enchantment (both clauses, 50% wins) ===\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse steel sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 G — payout 400 G (500 − 100 deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse dragon-material sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 G — 50% applies (500), then deductible (400)\");\n\n  // === Claim: Dragon + high enchantment exactly at threshold ===\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse dragon-material sword enchantment exactly 8 damage 1000 G — 500 G (50%) − 100 = 400 G payout\");\n\n  // === Claim: Deductible per damage