insurance sum for tracking. But the JSON spec says: quote result is `{premium: <integer>}`. The \"insurance sum\" and \"cap\" are internal tracking that matters for later claims. The test expects processScenario to track state between steps.\n\nSo: quote steps need to store insurance sum and cap information, and return them. But the spec says the output for quote is only `premium`. So the quote result is just premium. The insurance sum and cap need to be tracked internally for subsequent claim steps.\n\nFor tests 30 and 31, they might need the claim step to verify. Actually let me skip them for now and move to claim implementation. They require claim functionality. Let me implement claim processing.\n\nI need to:\n1. Track policy data (item list, insurance values) when a quote is processed\n2. Process claim steps against stored policies\n3. Return payouts and remaining cap\n\nLet me implement claims now. This is a big feature.\n\n## Major implementation: Claim processing"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4941cd9d66614eddb10786cc","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-28-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":258,"output":364,"cacheRead":118784,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":119406,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950681170,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-45193353-1ca4-485e-9ece-4a41346d24ff","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4941cd9d66614eddb10786cc","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number }[];\n}\n\ninterface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[] };\n}\n\ntype ScenarioStep = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ninterface ScenarioInput {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: ScenarioStep[];\n}\n\ninterface ScenarioResult {\n  results: ({ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number })[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst ALL_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\"sword\", \"amulet\", \"staff\", \"potion\", \"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst COMPONENT_BASE = 25;\nconst BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n\nfunction calculateQuotePremium(\n  items: { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number }[],\n  customerYears: number,\n  quoteIndex: number\n): number {\n  // Validate all item types\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (!ALL_ITEM_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n    }\n  }\n\n  let totalBase = 0;  // sum of raw base premiums (for policy modifiers)\n  let totalWithSurcharges = 0;  // sum including item-level surcharges\n  \n  // Group components for block pricing\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      const itemBase = BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n      let itemTotal = itemBase;\n      // Cursed surcharge: 50% of item base premium\n      if (item.cursed) {\n        itemTotal += itemBase * 0.5;\n      }\n      // High enchantment surcharge: 30% for enchantment level ≥ 5\n      if (item.enchantment !== undefined && item.enchantment >= 5) {\n        itemTotal += itemBase * 0.3;\n      }\n      totalBase += itemBase;\n      totalWithSurcharges += itemTotal;\n    }\n  }\n  \n  // Apply component block pricing: block of exactly 3 alike = 60 G\n  for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n    const componentTotal = count === 3 ? BLOCK_PRICE : count * COMPONENT_BASE;\n    totalBase += componentTotal;\n    totalWithSurcharges += componentTotal;\n  }\n  \n  // Policy-wide modifiers (additive, based on totalBase, not surcharged amounts)\n  let policyAdjustment = 0;\n  \n  // Loyalty discount: 20% for customers ≥ 2 years\n  if (customerYears >= 2) {\n    policyAdjustment -= totalBase * 0.2;\n  }\n  \n  // First insurance surcharge: 10%\n  policyAdjustment += totalBase * 0.1;\n  \n  // Follow-up contract discount: 15% for subsequent contracts\n  if (quoteIndex > 0) {\n    policyAdjustment -= totalBase * 0.15;\n  }\n\n  // Avoid floating-point rounding errors\n  const premium = Math.ceil(totalWithSurcharges + policyAdjustment + PROCESSING_FEE - 1e-10);\n  return premium;\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(input: ScenarioInput): ScenarioResult {\n  const results: ({ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number })[] = [];\n  let quoteIndex = 0;\n  \n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const premium = calculateQuotePremium(step.items, input.customer.yearsWithMHPCO, quoteIndex);\n      results.push({ premium });\n      quoteIndex++;\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950684418},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I need a massive overhaul to support claims. I need to:\n1. Track insurance values per item type\n2. Store policy data (items + insurance sum + cap) when a quote is processed\n3. Process claims: compute reimbursement per damage event, cap tracking\n\nLet me add the insurance values and claim processing:\n\nOrders of magnitude:\n- Insurance values: Sword=1000, Amulet=600, Staff=800, Potion=400, Component=250\n- Deductible: 100 per damage event  \n- Cap: 2x insurance sum\n- Enchantment ≥ 8: 50% reimbursement\n- Dragon material: full reimbursement\n- If both apply, 50% wins (dragon material only if enchantment < 8)\n\nLet"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_82ffb547fac549929a2a0a9f","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"const INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};","oldText":"const PROCESSINGaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1085,"output":373,"cacheRead":119296,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":120754,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950684420,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-a8fbf244-31ad-4941-afb2-7d6fe7a3323c","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_82ffb547fac549929a2a0a9f","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Validation failed for tool \"edit\":\n  - path: must have required properties path\n\nReceived arguments:\n{\n  \"edits\": [\n    {\n      \"newText\": \"const INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\\n  sword: 1000,\\n  amulet: 600,\\n  staff: 800,\\n  potion: 400,\\n  rune: 250,\\n  moonstone: 250,\\n};\",\n      \"oldText\": \"const PROCESSINGaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1784950687049},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edit error. Let me fix the malformed oldText:\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c4c60940b4ac445b9a8e1480","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-28-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"newText":"const INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;","oldText":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":495,"output":220,"cacheRead":120320,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":121035,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950687051,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-97491223-8ec6-4637-bc4d-9336d7d62179","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c4c60940b4ac445b9a8e1480","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-28-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  19 interface ScenarioResult {\n  20   results: ({ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number })[];\n  21 }\n  22 \n+ 23 const INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n+ 24   sword: 1000,\n+ 25   amulet: 600,\n+ 26   staff: 800,\n+ 27   potion: 400,\n+ 28   rune: 250,\n+ 29   moonstone: 250,\n+ 30 };\n+ 31 \n  23 const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n  24 \n  25 const BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  26   sword: 100,\n     ...","patch":"--- /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-28-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts\n+++ /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-28-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts\n@@ -19,8 +19,17 @@\n interface ScenarioResult {\n   results: ({ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number })[];\n }\n \n+const INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n+  sword: 1000,\n+  amulet: 600,\n+  staff: 800,\n+  potion: 400,\n+  rune: 250,\n+  moonstone: 250,\n+};\n+\n const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n \n const BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n   sword: 100,\n","firstChangedLine":23},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950689272},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I need to expand `processScenario` to handle claims. Let me add a policy data structure and claim processing:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_279481a7d00e47a58edabfc0","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"interface PolicyData {\n  items: { type: string; material?: string; enchantment?: number }[];\n  insuranceSum: number;\n  cap: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nfunction calculateItemInsuranceValue(itemType: string): number {\n  return INSURANCE_VALUES[itemType] ?? 0;\n}\n\nfunction computePayout(\n  damage: { itemType: string; amount: number },\n  policyItems: { type: string; material?: string; enchantment?: number }[]\n): number {\n  const policyItem = policyItems.find(i => i.type === damage.itemType);\n  if (!policyItem) {\n    throw new Error(`Item type not in policy: ${damage.itemType}`);\n  }\n  \n  const enchantment = policyItem.enchantment ?? 0;\n  const material = policyItem.material ?? \"\";\n  \n  let reimbursable = damage.amount;\n  \n  // Enchantment ≥ 8: 50% reimbursement\n  if (enchantment >= 8) {\n    reimbursable = Math.floor(reimbursable * 0.5);\n  } else if (material === \"dragon\") {\n    // Dragon material: full reimbursement\n    // (already at 100%)\n  }\n  // else: standard full reimbursement\n  \n  // Deductible: 100 G per damage event\n  reimbursable = reimbursable - 100;\n  \n  return Math.max(0, Math.floor(reimbursable));\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(input: ScenarioInput): ScenarioResult {\n  const results: ({ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number })[] = [];\n  const policies: PolicyData[] = [];\n  let quoteIndex = 0;\n  \n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const premium = calculateQuotePremium(step.items, input.customer.yearsWithMHPCO, quoteIndex);\n      \n      // Compute insurance sum and store policy\n      let insuranceSum = 0;\n      for (const item of step.items) {\n        insuranceSum += calculateItemInsuranceValue(item.type);\n      }\n      const cap = insuranceSum * 2;\n      policies.push({\n        items: step.items.map(i => ({ type: i.type, material: (i as any).material, enchantment: i.enchantment })),\n        insuranceSum,\n        cap,\n        remainingCap: cap,\n      });\n      \n      results.push({ premium });\n      quoteIndex++;\n    } else if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      const policy = policies[step.policy];\n      if (!policy) {\n        throw new Error(`Policy not found: ${step.policy}`);\n      }\n      \n      // Validate damages\n      for (const damage of step.incident.damages) {\n        if (damage.amount < 0) {\n          throw new Error(`Negative damage amount: ${damage.amount}`);\n        }\n        if (!ALL_ITEM_TYPES.has(damage.itemType)) {\n          throw new Error(`Unknown item type in claim: ${damage.itemType}`);\n        }\n        // Check count of damages per type vs policy coverage\n        const policyCount = policy.items.filter(i => i.type === damage.itemType).length;\n        const damageCount = step.incident.damages.filter(d => d.itemType === damage.itemType).length;\n        if (damageCount > policyCount) {\n          throw new Error(`More damage entries for \"${damage.itemType}\" than insured`);\n        }\n      }\n      \n      let totalPayout = 0;\n      for (const damage of step.incident.damages) {\n        totalPayout += calculatePayout(damage, policy.items);\n      }\n      \n      // Cap the payout\n      if (totalPayout > policy.remainingCap) {\n        totalPayout = policy.remainingCap;\n      }\n      \n      policy.remainingCap -= totalPayout;\n      results.push({ payout: totalPayout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n}","oldText":"function calculateQuotePremium(\n  items: { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number }[],\n  customerYears: number,\n  quoteIndex: number\n): number {\n  // Validate all item types\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (!ALL_ITEM_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n    }\n  }\n\n  let totalBase = 0;  // sum of raw base premiums (for policy modifiers)\n  let totalWithSurcharges = 0;  // sum including item-level surcharges\n  \n  // Group components for block pricing\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      const itemBase = BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n      let itemTotal = itemBase;\n      // Cursed surcharge: 50% of item base premium\n      if (item.cursed) {\n        itemTotal += itemBase * 0.5;\n      }\n      // High enchantment surcharge: 30% for enchantment level ≥ 5\n      if (item.enchantment !== undefined && item.enchantment >= 5) {\n        itemTotal += itemBase * 0.3;\n      }\n      totalBase += itemBase;\n      totalWithSurcharges += itemTotal;\n    }\n  }\n  \n  // Apply component block pricing: block of exactly 3 alike = 60 G\n  for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n    const componentTotal = count === 3 ? BLOCK_PRICE : count * COMPONENT_BASE;\n    totalBase += componentTotal;\n    totalWithSurcharges += componentTotal;\n  }\n  \n  // Policy-wide modifiers (additive, based on totalBase, not surcharged amounts)\n  let policyAdjustment = 0;\n  \n  // Loyalty discount: 20% for customers ≥ 2 years\n  if (customerYears >= 2) {\n    policyAdjustment -= totalBase * 0.2;\n  }\n  \n  // First insurance surcharge: 10%\n  policyAdjustment += totalBase * 0.1;\n  \n  // Follow-up contract discount: 15% for subsequent contracts\n  if (quoteIndex > 0) {\n    policyAdjustment -= totalBase * 0.15;\n  }\n\n  // Avoid floating-point rounding errors\n  const premium = Math.ceil(totalWithSurcharges + policyAdjustment + PROCESSING_FEE - 1e-10);\n  return premium;\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(input: ScenarioInput): ScenarioResult {\n  const results: ({ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number })[] = [];\n  let quoteIndex = 0;\n  \n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const premium = calculateQuotePremium(step.items, input.customer.yearsWithMHPCO, quoteIndex);\n      results.push({ premium });\n      quoteIndex++;\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n}"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-28-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":532,"output":1935,"cacheRead":120576,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":123043,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950689275,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-77b029fd-994b-41b5-8c72-93bff06767b8","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_279481a7d00e47a58edabfc0","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-28-59_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  45 \n  46 const COMPONENT_BASE = 25;\n  47 const BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n  48 \n- 49 function calculateQuotePremium(\n- 50   items: { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number }[],\n- 51   customerYears: number,\n- 52   quoteIndex: number\n+ 49 interface PolicyData {\n+ 50   items: { type: string; material?: string; enchantment?: number }[];\n+ 51   insuranceSum: number;\n+ 52   cap: number;\n+ 53   remainingCap: number;\n+ 54 }\n+ 55 \n+ 56 function calculateItemInsuranceValue(itemType: string): number {\n+ 57   return INSURANCE_VALUES[itemType] ?? 0;\n+ 58 }\n+ 59 \n+ 60 function computePayout(\n+ 61   damage: { itemType: string; amount: number },\n+ 62   policyItems: { type: string; material?: string; enchantment?: nu